# MCP Usage

Use MCPs only when they reduce context waste, improve precision, or prevent outdated implementation.

Do not add MCPs casually. Do not install or configure MCPs unless explicitly asked.

Do not commit secrets, production credentials, service-role keys, or broad write-access config.

Prefer read-only or explicit-approval access for Supabase and GitHub style operations.

Project-local files remain canonical; MCP outputs are evidence, not source of truth.
